#4471 is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Sorted by tenant locale and booking form instead of
by subject line, the reports merged into it are **two separate problems**, and only one of them is
the bug this ticket is about.

## How the pile splits

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Ticket 1 · `parser` · 379 reports

The shared date parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes dates day
first (`locales.ts` keeps the directory), so invites the tenants sent come back flipped: 7 April runs on
4 July. Eleven tenants, all three channels (app 204 · email 150 · form 25), April → October. This is the
bug the desk already knows, and the reason #4471 exists. Filing note: `desk-notes.json` lets five
reports the desk read as a one-day move stay where they are filed, as footnotes under this cause.

## Ticket 2 · `hint` · 33 reports

All of these came through the **booking-v3** form. Its hint prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, so guests type
month first, and the form reads what arrived the tenant's way — day first. Same flipped day, wrong
entry and wrong hint, so a different fix. The three tenants in this group — alder.physio,
copper.studio, pale.harbour — are exactly the three running booking-v3. Every other tenant runs
booking-v2, whose hint says `DD/MM/YYYY`, so their form reports belong to the parser cause.

## Filed

One ticket per problem, with these counts, in the public GitHub repo linked from the kb README.

<Callout>
Fed only subject lines, every report matches one open ticket. Fed the tenant's locale and form,
the pile sorts into two problems. Read the report, then merge it.
</Callout>

